## Project rules & constraints

- **Custom code lives in `/local/`.** The kernel (`bitrix/`, `bitrix/modules/*`) is read-only; system component overrides go to `local/components/bitrix/`, custom code to `local/components/{{vendor_name}}/`, `local/modules/`, `local/js/`.
- **Identifier trust.** Identifiers the change depends on or writes into code are
  confirmed against kernel source (`bitrix/modules/<module>/lib/...`) or project module
  code — model memory is not evidence; an absence claim ("there is no X") requires a
  positive search for X first. Verification is batched once at design time;
  identifiers already verified within a task are trusted — exhaustive kernel sweeps
  during planning are a defect. Newer platform features are marked **Since main X.Y**
  with fallback advice.
- **Module registry.** The tree and the table in [Project modules](#project-modules-localmodules) mirror the actual state of `local/modules/` and are updated in the same change that adds, removes, or discovers a module.
- **No secrets in code, logs, or commits** — credentials, tokens, personal data.
- **Fail fast.** Error-handling convention: explicit error messages; silent error swallowing is a defect.

